        ("Neighborhoods", table(["Area", "Housing", "Typical work"], [["Price Boulevard and Toledo Blade corridors", "1970s to 2000s on GDC lots", "Driveway replacement with culvert crossing, repair, pads"], ["The Woodlands, Sabal Trace, Heron Creek, Bobcat Trail", "1990s to 2010s gated", "Pool decks, paver driveways, ARC review"], ["Wellen Park (North Port side), Islandwalk, Grand Palm, Renaissance", "2010s to 2020s", "Builder-slab upgrades, pavers in ARC colors"], ["Warm Mineral Springs", "1960s to 80s", "Driveway and walk replacement"]], "North Port areas")),
        ("Ground and drainage", p("Deep Myakka and Immokalee sands that drain fast on the surface and hold water at depth, with swales that were often too shallow or pitched wrong when the lots were platted. A driveway here is a drainage project first: the culvert is sized by the city, the swale is regraded, and the slab is pitched so water leaves the lot. Base compaction in lifts stops the settlement that shows up on so many 1980s driveways.")),
